<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">24 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 24 October, from 1260 to 2003.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/baybars" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baybars.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1260">1260 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">766 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Baybars seizes the Mamluk throne after Qutuz is assassinated</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Shortly after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qutuz">Qutuz</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a> defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ain-jalut">Ain Jalut</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Qutuz was assassinated, and Baybars seized the throne as the fourth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>. He reigned until 1277.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qutuz">Qutuz</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1273">1273 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">753 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rudolf of Habsburg is crowned King of the Romans at Aachen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-i-of-germany">Rudolf of Habsburg</a>, a Swabian count elected King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> that year, was crowned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aachen-cathedral">Aachen Cathedral</a>, the first of his house to hold the title. His election ended the Great Interregnum after the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-i-of-germany">Rudolf I of Germany</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1360">1360 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">666 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Treaty of Brétigny is ratified at Calais</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Edward III and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-ii-of-france">John II of France</a> ratified at Calais the peace agreed at Brétigny in May. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> gained Aquitaine and Calais in full <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> and a huge ransom for the captured French king, pausing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1648">1648 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">378 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Peace of Westphalia ends the Thirty Years' War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Treaties signed at Münster and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osnabruck">Osnabrück</a> ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a>, which had devastated central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. The settlement confirmed the autonomy of the German princes and recognised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> and Swiss independence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1789">1789 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">237 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Brabant Revolution begins in the Austrian Netherlands</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An émigré army from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> invaded the Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, beginning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brabant-revolution">Brabant Revolution</a> against Emperor Joseph II's centralising and church reforms. The rebels drove out the Austrian forces and in January 1790 proclaimed the United Belgian States.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brabant-revolution">Brabant Revolution</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1929">1929 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">97 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Black Thursday: panic selling hits Wall Street</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Nearly 13 million shares changed hands as panic swept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> Stock Exchange. Bankers briefly steadied prices, but the crash that followed the next week opened the way to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-depression">Great Depression</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The United Nations comes into being</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations-charter">United Nations Charter</a> entered into force once a majority of signatories, including the five permanent Security Council members, had ratified it. The date is celebrated annually as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> Day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2003">2003 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">23 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Concorde makes its last commercial flight</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British Airways Concorde flight BA002 from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> landed at Heathrow, ending 27 years of supersonic passenger travel. The aircraft could cross the Atlantic in about three and a half hours.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li></ol>
